 Timer;ticks;elapsed;Assert;until
 ⍝ Note: This will not work properly until Dyalog changes to allow ⎕WGIVE-like handling as well as events happening during ⎕DL.

 '#'∆WI Pass MT⊢'Reset' ⍝ Clean out any previous GUI work
 Assert←⊢Pass 1

 't'∆WI Pass(,'t')⊢'Create' 'Timer'
 't'∆WI Pass 1⊢'enabled'
 't'∆WI Pass 1000⊢'interval'
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'enabled' 0
 't'∆WI Pass 0⊢'enabled'
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'onTimer' 'ticks,←1000|∆WARG÷1000' ⍝ Just make a note any time it ticks

 ticks←⍬
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'interval' 500 ⍝ Speed at which tests are performed
 elapsed←⎕AI[3]
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'enabled' 1
 ⎕DL 2 ⍝ Wait quietly for 2 seconds
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'enabled' 0
 elapsed←⎕AI[3]-elapsed
 Assert elapsed≥2
 ⍝? Assert ticks≢⍛∊4 ⍝? Not functioning in Dyalog
 ⍝? 'Separation =',⍕¯2-/ticks

 ticks←⍬
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'interval' 500 ⍝ Speed at which tests are performed
 until←⎕AI[3]+2000 ⍝ A 2-second delay
 elapsed←⎕AI[3]
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'enabled' 1
 :While ⎕AI[3]<until
    ⍝ Just wait here in a hard loop for 2 seconds
 :EndWhile
 't'∆WI Pass MT⊢'enabled' 0
 elapsed←⎕AI[3]-elapsed
 Assert elapsed≥2
 Assert 0=≢ticks ⍝ Nothing should be firing during this loop, without ⎕WGIVE

⍝? We'll also need to repeat the above loop, with ⎕WGIVE 0/#, once Dyalog can support that functionality

⍝? We might also be able to test timers that happen while ⎕DQ is active, but that's going to take a good bit more coordination


quit:
 '#'∆WI Pass MT⊢'Reset' ⍝ Clean up after tests


⍝? Note: We need to do a lot of "when does a timer fire" work so see if we can the event to happen like APL+Win, i.e. when the system is otherwise waiting
⍝? Question (both systems): If you disable a running timer during a tick and then reenable it later, does it resume where it left off or start counting over?
